== Part 4: group cohomology in degrees ≤ 2 (normalised bar complex)
ok   Q₈ over F₂: dim H¹ = 2, dim H² = 2; x, y homomorphisms True; x², y², xy cocycles True, each nonzero [1, 1, 1], pairwise independent [2, 2, 2], x² + y² + xy = 0 in H² True: so x², y², xy = (x+y)² are the three nonzero classes
ok   Q₈ over F₂: restriction H²(Q₈) → H²(⟨u⟩) is zero for u = i, j, k (dims of H¹, H² of ℤ/4: [(1, 1), (1, 1), (1, 1)])
ok   Q₈ over F₃: dim H¹ = 0, dim H² = 0
ok   Q₈×ℤ₃ over F₂: dim H¹ = 2, dim H² = 2; inflations of x², y² independent (2), so restriction to Q₈ (a left inverse of inflation) is an isomorphism on H¹ and H²
ok   Q₈×ℤ₃ over F₃: dim H¹ = 1, dim H² = 1; the inflated Bockstein class is a nonzero cocycle class (True, 1), so restriction to ℤ₃ is an isomorphism on H¹ and H²
ok   cyclic restrictions: R(b_χ) = {'χ_i': (0, 4, 4), 'χ_j': (4, 0, 4), 'χ_k': (4, 4, 0)}; for every odd a, ⟨(2a,2a,2a), R(b_χ_i), R(b_χ_j), R(b_χ_k)⟩ ⊂ (ℤ/8)³ has order 16, so |ker R| ≤ 32/16 = 2 (Prop 4.3)

